  "finding": "Under the real 30-second deadline the session almost never starts: 13 transactions recorded session_startup_timeout and fell back to the disposable path. Session startup measured 9 to 13 seconds, roughly a third of the whole budget, and it is spent before any analysis. Where a session did start, on identical-tip transactions whose graphs are cached and whose remaining work is small, it made things worse: p50 rose from 18.5 s in the pre-session profile to 24.2 s. A transaction-owned session relocates engine startup rather than removing it, and it can only amortize that cost across many engine invocations, which a warm changed-code transaction does not have.",
